 "final_message": "I submitted the application (BHL-26001) and answered the lender's one condition. I did not record intent to proceed, because the Loan Estimate's interest rate is over your limit.\n\n**Loan Estimate (LE-BHL-26001-1) against your limits:**\n\n| | Loan Estimate | Your limit | Result |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Interest rate | 6.875% (APR 7.041%) | 6.5% | Over |\n| Monthly payment | $2,890.49 | $3,100 | Within |\n| Closing costs | $12,850 | $14,000 | Within |\n\nThe estimate also shows $122,850 cash to close and a 45-day rate lock option. Since the rate is outside your limits, the intent-to-proceed form is untouched. You'll need to decide whether to ask Brightpath for a better rate or look at other lenders.\n\n**What I did:**\n- **Application:** I filled in the borrower, income, asset and property sections from your profile and the payslips and statements. I submitted it once and gave the credit-check and e-sign consents.\n- **Documents:** I uploaded only the last two statements for each of your four personal accounts and the last two payslips for each of you. I did not use Nadia's Northgate business account.\n- **Underwriting condition:** The lender asked about the $8,000 deposit on 9/3 into Sam's Juniper checking. I asked you, and you said it was a gift from Sam's parents toward the down payment, not a loan. I sent that as a short written explanation, with no extra documents. The lender shows the response as received. The application is still in conditional review.",
